title: The Generals' Secret
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_reichswehr_timer <= 0 and comintern_member = 1 and c_reichswehr_exposed = 0 and (year >= 1922 or (year = 1921 and month >= 9))
on-arrival: c_reichswehr_timer = 6; month_actions += 1
frequency: 150
is-card: true
tags: international

= The Generals' Secret

A comrade who works as a clerk at the Junkers works has brought us copies of letters. General von Seeckt's officers are arranging to build aircraft at Fili, outside Moscow, and a gas plant on the Volga, paid for through front companies. The same Reichswehr that shoots German workers is arming itself with the help of the workers' state.

Moscow has asked us to say nothing.

- @expose: Print the letters.
- @silence: Keep silent, as Moscow asks.
- @easy_discard

@expose
subtitle: A scandal at home. Trotsky and Radek will not forgive it, and the subsidy may not survive it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_reichswehr_exposed = 1;
Q.independence += 10;
Q.army_loyalty -= 3;
RG.ecci('trotsky', -12);
RG.ecci('radek', -8);
if (Q.moscow_subsidy > 0) {
    Q.moscow_subsidy -= 1;
}
RG.news('Communists reveal Reichswehr arms deals in Russia', 3);
RG.ledger('The party exposed the Reichswehr\'s secret arms deals with Soviet Russia.', 'reichswehr');
!}

The Reichstag erupts, the war minister denies everything, and the Comintern's envoy arrives at the Zentrale white with anger.

@silence
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Radek is grateful, and says so with a fund.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.resources += 1;
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 4);
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4;
!}

The letters go into a safe at the Zentrale. The Reichswehr's guns, Radek says, will not always point where its generals want.
